{"id":"mahabharata-7-083","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":83,"title":"त्र्यशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 83 · Ghatotkacha and Alambusha","summary":{"en":"Ashvatthaman, Duryodhana and others wound the sons of Draupadi, while Bhima and Ghatotkacha fight the rakshasa Alambusha in a wild combat. Ghatotkacha takes many shapes and voices, and Bhima's son is praised.","kn":"ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಮೊದಲಾದವರು ದ್ರೌಪದೇಯರನ್ನು ಗಾಯಗೊಳಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಭೀಮ-ಘಟೋತ್ಕಚರು ರಾಕ್ಷಸ ಅಲಂಬುಷನೊಡನೆ ಉಗ್ರವಾಗಿ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಘಟೋತ್ಕಚ ಅನೇಕ ರೂಪ, ಧ್ವನಿಗಳನ್ನು ತಾಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अश्वत्थामा, दुर्योधन आदि द्रौपदी के पुत्रों को घायल करते हैं, और भीम और घटोत्कच राक्षस अलम्बुष से भयंकर युद्ध करते हैं। घटोत्कच अनेक रूप और स्वर धारण करता है।","te":"అశ్వత్థామ, దుర్యోధనుడు తదితరులు ద్రౌపదేయులను గాయపరుస్తారు; భీమ ఘటోత్కచులు రాక్షసుడు అలంబుషునితో భీకరంగా పోరాడతారు. ఘటోత్కచుడు అనేక రూపాలు, స్వరాలు ధరిస్తాడు.","ta":"அஸ்வத்தாமன், துரியோதனன் முதலியோர் திரௌபதியின் மக்களைக் காயப்படுத்துகின்றனர்; பீமனும் கடோத்கசனும் அரக்கன் அலம்புசனுடன் கடும்போர் புரிகின்றனர். கடோத்கசன் பல உருவங்களையும் குரல்களையும் எடுக்கிறான்.","ml":"അശ്വത്ഥാമാവും ദുര്യോധനനും മറ്റുള്ളവരും ദ്രൗപദിയുടെ പുത്രന്മാരെ മുറിവേൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു; ഭീമനും ഘടോൽക്കചനും രാക്ഷസനായ അലംബുഷനോട് കാട്ടുയുദ്ധം ചെയ്യുന്നു. ഘടോൽക്കചൻ പല രൂപങ്ങളിലും ശബ്ദങ്ങളിലും പ്രത്യക്ഷപ്പെടുന്നു; ഭീമന്റെ പുത്രൻ പ്രശംസിക്കപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.83; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"द्रौपदेयान्महेष्वासान्सौमदत्तिर्महायशाः ।\nएकैकं पञ्चभिर्विद्ध्वा पुनर्विव्याध सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Somadatta's glorious son Bhurishravas pierced each of the mighty-bowman sons of Draupadi with five arrows, and then struck each again with seven."}},{"n":2,"text":"ते पीडिता भृशं तेन रौद्रेण सहसा विभो ।\nप्रमूढा नैव विविदुर्मृधे कृत्यं स्म किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hard pressed all at once by that fierce warrior, O lord, they were bewildered and could not tell what to do in the fight."}},{"n":3,"text":"नाकुलिस्तु शतानीकः सौमदत्तिं नरर्षभम् ।\nद्वाभ्यां विद्ध्वानदद्धृष्टः शराभ्यां शत्रुतापनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shatanika, Nakula's son, a tormentor of foes, pierced that bull among men, Somadatta's son, with two arrows and roared in delight."}},{"n":4,"text":"तथेतरे रणे यत्तास्त्रिभिस्त्रिभिरजिह्मगैः ।\nविव्यधुः समरे तूर्णं सौमदत्तिममर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The others too, intent in the battle, each quickly struck the wrathful son of Somadatta with three straight arrows."}},{"n":5,"text":"स तान्प्रति महाराज चिक्षिपे पञ्च सायकान् ।\nएकैकं हृदि चाजघ्ने एकैकेन महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, he shot five arrows back at them, and that man of great fame struck each in the heart with one."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततस्ते भ्रातरः पञ्च शरैर्विद्धा महात्मना ।\nपरिवार्य रथैर्वीरं विव्यधुः सायकैर्भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the five brothers, wounded by that great-souled man, surrounded the hero with their chariots and pounded him with arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"आर्जुनिस्तु हयांस्तस्य चतुर्भिर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nप्रेषयामास संक्रुद्धो यमस्य सदनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna's son, furious, sent the four horses of Somadatta's son to the abode of Yama with four sharp arrows."}},{"n":8,"text":"भैमसेनिर्धनुश्छित्त्वा सौमदत्तेर्महात्मनः ।\nननाद बलवन्नादं विव्याध च शितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima's son cut the bow of the great-souled son of Somadatta, let out a mighty roar, and struck him with sharp arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"यौधिष्ठिरो ध्वजं तस्य छित्त्वा भूमावपातयत् ।\nनाकुलिश्चाश्वयन्तारं रथनीडादपाहरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira's son cut down his banner and threw it to the ground, and Nakula's son pulled his charioteer from the chariot's seat."}},{"n":10,"text":"साहदेविस्तु तं ज्ञात्वा भ्रातृभिर्विमुखीकृतम् ।\nक्षुरप्रेण शिरो राजन्निचकर्त महामनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sahadeva's son, noble in mind, seeing him turned away by his brothers, cut off his head with a razor-headed arrow, O king."}},{"n":11,"text":"तच्छिरो न्यपतद्भूमौ तपनीयविभूषितम् ।\nभ्राजयन्तं रणोद्देशं बालसूर्यसमप्रभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That head, adorned with gold, fell to the ground and lit up that part of the battlefield with a glow like the young sun."}},{"n":12,"text":"सौमदत्तेः शिरो दृष्ट्वा निपतत्तन्महात्मनः ।\nवित्रस्तास्तावका राजन्प्रदुद्रुवुरनेकधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the great-souled man's head fall, your soldiers, O king, were terrified and fled in many directions."}},{"n":13,"text":"अलम्बुसस्तु समरे भीमसेनं महाबलम् ।\nयोधयामास संक्रुद्धो लक्ष्मणं रावणिर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alambusha, in a rage, fought the mighty Bhimasena in the battle, as Ravana's son once fought Lakshmana."}},{"n":14,"text":"संप्रयुद्धौ रणे दृष्ट्वा तावुभौ नरराक्षसौ ।\nविस्मयः सर्वभूतानां प्रहर्षश्चाभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Watching those two, a man and a rakshasa, locked in combat, all beings felt both wonder and delight."}},{"n":15,"text":"आर्ष्यशृङ्गिं ततो भीमो नवभिर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nविव्याध प्रहसन्राजन्राक्षसेन्द्रममर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, almost laughing, pierced Alambusha, the wrathful lord of rakshasas and son of Rishyashringa, with nine sharp arrows, O king."}},{"n":16,"text":"तद्रक्षः समरे विद्धं कृत्वा नादं भयावहम् ।\nअभ्यद्रवत्ततो भीमं ये च तस्य पदानुगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wounded in the battle, that rakshasa let out a terrifying cry and rushed at Bhima, together with his followers."}},{"n":17,"text":"स भीमं पञ्चभिर्विद्ध्वा शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nभीमानुगाञ्जघानाशु रथांस्त्रिंशदरिंदमः ।\nपुनश्चतुःशतान्हत्वा भीमं विव्याध पत्रिणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"That tamer of foes pierced Bhima with five straight-jointed arrows and quickly killed thirty chariots of Bhima's followers; then, after killing four hundred more, he struck Bhima with a feathered shaft."}},{"n":18,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धस्तदा भीमो राक्षसेन महाबलः ।\nनिषसाद रथोपस्थे मूर्छयाभिपरिप्लुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Badly wounded by the rakshasa, the mighty Bhima sank down on the seat of his chariot, overcome by a faint."}},{"n":19,"text":"प्रतिलभ्य ततः संज्ञां मारुतिः क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nविकृष्य कार्मुकं घोरं भारसाधनमुत्तमम् ।\nअलम्बुसं शरैस्तीक्ष्णैरर्दयामास सर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regaining consciousness, Maruti's son, dizzy with rage, drew his terrible bow, the best for carrying a heavy load, and tormented Alambusha on every side with sharp arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"स विद्धो बहुभिर्बाणैर्नीलाञ्जनचयोपमः ।\nशुशुभे सर्वतो राजन्प्रदीप्त इव किंशुकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by many arrows, he looked like a heap of dark collyrium, and shone on every side, O king, like a blazing kimshuka tree."}},{"n":21,"text":"स वध्यमानः समरे भीमचापच्युतैः शरैः ।\nस्मरन्भ्रातृवधं चैव पाण्डवेन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he was being struck in battle by arrows loosed from Bhima's bow, remembering how the great-souled Pandava had killed his brother,"}},{"n":22,"text":"घोरं रूपमथो कृत्वा भीमसेनमभाषत ।\nतिष्ठेदानीं रणे पार्थ पश्य मेऽद्य पराक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He took on a terrible form and said to Bhimasena, \"Stay there now in battle, son of Pritha, and see my prowess today."}},{"n":23,"text":"बको नाम सुदुर्बुद्धे राक्षसप्रवरो बली ।\nपरोक्षं मम तद्वृत्तं यद्भ्राता मे हतस्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fool, a mighty rakshasa chief named Baka was my kinsman. You killed my brother, when I was out of sight."}},{"n":24,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो भीममन्तर्धानगतस्तदा ।\nमहाता शरवर्षेण भृशं तं समवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to Bhima, he vanished, and showered him heavily with a great rain of arrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"भीमस्तु समरे राजन्नदृश्ये राक्षसे तदा ।\nआकाशं पूरयामास शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Bhima, O king, with the rakshasa invisible, filled the sky with straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":26,"text":"स वध्यमानो भीमेन निमेषाद्रथमास्थितः ।\nजगाम धरणीं क्षुद्रः खं चैव सहसागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by Bhima, that mean creature in an instant got back into his chariot, then went down to the earth and suddenly up into the sky."}},{"n":27,"text":"उच्चावचानि रूपाणि चकार सुबहूनि च ।\nउच्चावचास्तथा वाचो व्याजहार समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He assumed many forms, high and low, and uttered many kinds of speech, loud and soft, on every side."}},{"n":28,"text":"तेन पाण्डवसैन्यानां मृदिता युधि वारणाः ।\nहयाश्च बहवो राजन्पत्तयश्च तथा पुनः ।\nरथेभ्यो रथिनः पेतुस्तस्य नुन्नाः स्म सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By him the elephants, horses and foot soldiers of the Pandava armies were crushed in the battle, and chariot-fighters, struck by his arrows, fell from their chariots."}},{"n":29,"text":"शोणितोदां रथावर्तां हस्तिग्राहसमाकुलाम् ।\nछत्रहंसां कर्दमिनीं बाहुपन्नगसंकुलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He made a river flow that ran with blood, with chariots for whirlpools and elephants for crocodiles, umbrellas for swans, mud for banks, and arms for snakes,"}},{"n":30,"text":"नदीं प्रवर्तयामास रक्षोगणसमाकुलाम् ।\nवहन्तीं बहुधा राजंश्चेदिपाञ्चालसृञ्जयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Crowded with rakshasa hordes, carrying away in many ways the Chedis, Panchalas and Srinjayas, O king."}},{"n":31,"text":"तं तथा समरे राजन्विचरन्तमभीतवत् ।\nपाण्डवा भृशसंविग्नाः प्रापश्यंस्तस्य विक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he roamed the battle fearlessly, O king, the Pandavas, deeply distressed, watched his might."}},{"n":32,"text":"तावकानां तु सैन्यानां प्रहर्षः समजायत ।\nवादित्रनिनदश्चोग्रः सुमहाँल्लोमहर्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joy rose among your troops, and a fierce, very loud, hair-raising din of instruments sounded."}},{"n":33,"text":"तं श्रुत्वा निनदं घोरं तव सैन्यस्य पाण्डवः ।\nनामृष्यत यथा नागस्तलशब्दं समीरितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that dreadful noise from your army, the Pandava could not bear it, as an elephant cannot bear a slap on the ground."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततः क्रोधाभिताम्राक्षो निर्दहन्निव पावकः ।\nसंदधे त्वाष्ट्रमस्त्रं स स्वयं त्वष्टेव मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, his eyes red with fury, burning as it were like fire, he took up the Tvashtri weapon, himself like Tvashtri, O lord."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततः शरसहस्राणि प्रादुरासन्समन्ततः ।\nतैः शरैस्तव सैन्यस्य विद्रावः सुमहानभूत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of arrows then appeared on every side, and by those arrows your army was greatly routed."}},{"n":36,"text":"तदस्त्रं प्रेषितं तेन भीमसेनेन संयुगे ।\nराक्षसस्य महामायां हत्वा राक्षसमार्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That weapon sent by Bhimasena in the battle destroyed the rakshasa's great illusion and crushed the rakshasa himself."}},{"n":37,"text":"स वध्यमानो बहुधा भीमसेनेन राक्षसः ।\nसंत्यज्य संयुगे भीमं द्रोणानीकमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck in many ways by Bhimasena, the rakshasa abandoned Bhima in the battle and fled to Drona's division."}},{"n":38,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु निर्जिते राजन्राक्षसेन्द्रे महात्मना ।\nअनादयन्सिंहनादैः पाण्डवाः सर्वतोदिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that lord of rakshasas was beaten by the great-souled Bhima, O king, the Pandavas roared lion-roars in all directions."}},{"n":39,"text":"अपूजयन्मारुतिं च संहृष्टास्ते महाबलम् ।\nप्रह्रादं समरे जित्वा यथा शक्रं मरुद्गणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Overjoyed, they praised the mighty son of Maruti, as the Maruts praised Indra when he defeated Prahlada in battle."}}]}]}